WEBVTT

00:00:03.437 --> 00:00:06.606
In this short film, you will learn about
how your urinary system

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.943
works, the different parts of your body
that are involved,

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:13.413
and the different functions
they each have.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.850
The urinary system filters and excretes
waste.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.952
It's made up of two parts.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:24.024
The upper urinary system, which includes
the kidneys and your ureters.

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.892
The kidneys filter your blood of excess

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:30.063
fluid and impurities,
which then becomes urine.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.199
The ureters are tubes that transport urine

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:35.268
from the kidneys to the bladder.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.304
There is a valve within the ureters

00:00:37.304 --> 00:00:40.273
that prevents urine back
flowing to the kidneys.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:46.246
The backflow of the urine
could cause damage to the kidneys.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.647
The lower urinary system

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:52.152
includes the bladder,
the urethra and the sphincter muscles.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:56.923
The female adult urethra is somewhere
between three and five centimeters long.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:01.394
It's a tube between the bladder
and the opening of the urethra.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.729
The bladder is a hollow,

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:06.833
muscular
organ made up of several muscle layers.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.102
The bladders main function is to store

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:13.006
and eliminate urine.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.508
The bladder receives signals

00:01:14.508 --> 00:01:17.911
as it fills with urine to indicate
the need to urinate.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:22.082
When the bladder is about halfway
full, around 250 milliliters,

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:26.052
you get the first sensation
you need to urinate.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.155
As the bladder continues to fill,

00:01:28.155 --> 00:01:32.626
the sensation becomes stronger
and the urgency to urinate increases.

00:01:32.626 --> 00:01:38.064
The bladder muscles relax as your bladder
fills, but contract when you urinate.

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:41.334
The sphincter muscle controls
flow of urine out of the bladder,

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:45.739
which squeezes the urethra shut
as the bladder fills and relaxes.

00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:49.509
As the bladder is emptied.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.679
To summarize, the urinary system
is made up of two parts,

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:55.982
which includes the upper and lower system,
and both play

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.982
an important role in production
and excretion of urine from the body.
